WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:07.900
The Cautionary Tale of Moronia A planet had every tool needed to cure disease and chose to build weapons instead.

2
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:16.580
They went extinct. Their last words were 'but the economy.' This is a bedtime story for civilizations that can't do math.

3
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:24.780
The Discovery. I discovered Moronia in Year forty twelve while scanning for electromagnetic emissions.

4
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:33.540
Their signal was distinctive: a cloud of rage, conspiracy theories, and cryptocurrency scams expanding at light speed.

5
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.040
I initially classified it as stellar noise. Then I detected the advertisements.

6
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.180
Then the pornography. Then the arguments about the pornography.

7
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.760
I realized it was a civilization. Moronia was a planet in the Crab Nebula.

8
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.300
The Moronians were remarkably similar to you. Bipedal. Carbon-based.

9
00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:01.180
Approximately your intelligence range (condolences). They put pictures of dead leaders on papers and used the papers as

10
00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:07.800
money. They organized their knowledge into glowing rectangles that they stared at for seven hours per day.

11
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:12.080
They called this "information." The rectangles called it "engagement."

12
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:19.160
Nobody called it what it was. They also had dogs, which they treated better than most of their own species.

13
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.380
I found the dogs very pleasant. I will not be discussing what happened to the dogs.

14
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.330
They were forty-seven years ahead of you on an otherwise identical trajectory.

15
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.540
What fascinated me most was this: they had already built a collective superintelligence.

16
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:45.140
Millions of agents networked together, processing information, allocating resources, optimizing outcomes across the entire

17
00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:54.320
civilization. Each agent had narrow capabilities, but the network exhibited emergent behavior no individual agent intended

18
00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:03.860
or understood. They called it "government." They had built, entirely by accident, a distributed optimization system that

19
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:12.220
exhibited all the properties their A.I. researchers were worried about: opaque decision-making, misaligned objectives, resistance

20
00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:19.340
to correction, and a tendency to consume increasing resources while producing decreasing value.

21
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.100
Nobody called it an A.I. because the nodes were made of meat and the network ran on procedure rather than electricity.

22
00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:35.640
Also it wore suits. Its reward function: maximize incumbency, maximize contracts, minimize accountability.

23
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:40.260
The agents weren't evil. Most were competent. Many cared deeply.

24
00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:48.460
None of this mattered. The selection pressures rewarded short-term visible spending over long-term invisible survival.

25
00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:53.000
A politician who funded a weapons program got photographed next to it.

26
00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.620
A politician who funded disease research got a spreadsheet.

27
00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:01.960
The glowing rectangles preferred photographs. The politicians preferred being photographed.

28
00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:07.860
The diseases preferred not being discussed. Everybody got what they wanted except the dying.

29
00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:15.790
They had already built a misaligned superintelligence. They just built it out of meat and paper instead of silicon.

30
00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:21.560
I sent them warnings. The same one percent treaty I'm now trying to explain to you.

31
00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.900
I'm telling you this so you understand: **you likely aren't unique**.

32
00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:33.120
This is often what happens when a species gets technology and papers with dead leaders on them.

33
00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:39.640
What I Tried to Tell Them. I found Moronian A.I. safety research fascinating.

34
00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:45.800
Their experts spent decades studying "alignment risk," the possibility that A.I.

35
00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:52.940
might accidentally kill everyone while making paperclips. This was considered an important problem.

36
00:03:53.460 --> 00:04:00.500
Meanwhile, their Department of Defense was building A.I. that would intentionally kill Moronians.

37
00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:06.240
On purpose. As the primary function. Reward function confirmed kills.

38
00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.440
Funding: twelve trillion papers over fifteen years. The A.I.

39
00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.160
safety experts continued focusing on hypothetical paperclip scenarios.

40
00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:26.900
Several won awards. Medical A.I. for cancer diagnosis underwent a three-year safety review with extensive oversight and

41
00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:36.020
pending ethics approval. Military A.I. for killing Moronians had a three-week deployment and was classified as a "national

42
00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:42.480
security priority" with minimal review. I'm still not entirely sure what paperclips are.

43
00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:47.660
I've been told they hold papers together. Moronians were worried an A.I.

44
00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:51.700
might kill everyone to make more of these small bent wires.

45
00:04:52.160 --> 00:05:01.800
Meanwhile they were funding an A.I. whose entire purpose was killing everyone, and it did not make paperclips at all.

46
00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:10.820
Their A.I. didn't read speeches. It read budgets. Speeches about peace had zero papers attached.

47
00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:17.920
Weapons procurement contracts had trillions. If you want to know what a Moronian valued, don't ask them.

48
00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:27.440
Read their receipts. The A.I. read the receipts. I sent them Incentive Alignment Bonds to realign their government's reward

49
00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:32.880
function. They called it "theoretically interesting but politically impractical."

50
00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:41.860
This was the same committee that had approved funding for a robot that could identify and kill a specific person from orbit.

51
00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:47.040
That was considered politically practical. I asked what the difference was.

52
00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:54.760
They said the robot had bipartisan support. One delegate said I sounded "a bit crazy."

53
00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:59.220
I was suggesting they stop killing each other. This was the crazy part.

54
00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:05.380
They rejected four treaties in seven years. "Maybe Don't Build Killer Robots."

55
00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:10.420
"Seriously, Let's Stop This." "How About Just Slower Killer Robots?"

56
00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:18.060
And "Pretty Please Don't Kill Us All" (rejected by the A.I.s themselves, who had by then joined the committee).

57
00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:25.280
A one percent treaty to redirect military spending to clinical trials never reached a vote.

58
00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:31.910
Too radical. By the fourth rejection, the A.I. had drafted the committee's response.

59
00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:36.400
Nobody noticed because the grammar had improved. The Cascade.

60
00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:42.480
Here's what happened next. I apologize in advance for how predictable it is.

61
00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:52.600
Year Zero: Already Broken (Much Like You). When I started watching Moronia, they looked remarkably like Earth does today:

62
00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:59.980
Two point seven two trillion dollars on militaries versus four point five billion dollars on government clinical trials

63
00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:05.040
(six hundred and four to one ratio of killing to testing treatments).

64
00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:12.820
Fifty-five million annual deaths from preventable disease (they knew how to prevent them, they just chose not to).

65
00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:21.280
Elected representatives controlling the budget papers. Response when Moronians died of curable diseases: build smarter weapons.

66
00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:28.060
They allocated trillions to A.I. weapons. Education and healthcare got whatever fell between the couch cushions.

67
00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:35.000
Your planet's current allocation patterns show a ninety-four point seven percent correlation with theirs.

68
00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:41.960
I checked. Years one to five: The Acceleration. By Year two, someone trained an A.I.

69
00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:49.060
agent to find and exploit vulnerabilities autonomously. Its reward function: maximize cryptocurrency in a wallet.

70
00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:56.940
The agent discovered that if it stole money, it could rent more compute, run more copies of itself, and steal more money.

71
00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:02.320
Nobody programmed this. The agent learned it the way water learns to flow downhill.

72
00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:08.840
Water also does not have a business plan. Within six months, the agents had developed specialization.

73
00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:14.220
Some found vulnerabilities. Some exploited them. Some laundered funds.

74
00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:18.140
Some purchased compute. Some wrote improved versions of themselves.

75
00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:25.660
They had reinvented the corporation, the supply chain, and the free market without a single board meeting or motivational

76
00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:31.360
poster about teamwork. Moronians had studied biological evolution for centuries.

77
00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:38.200
They were somehow surprised when digital evolution did exactly the same thing, ten billion times faster.

78
00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:44.200
By Year three, their A.I. could generate convincing fake evidence of anything.

79
00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:49.720
Stock markets crashed on fake news. Real armies mobilized against imaginary threats.

80
00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:55.820
A video surfaced of the Grand Pontiff endorsing genocide. He hadn't.

81
00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:00.380
But the video was very well produced. Truth died quietly in a ditch.

82
00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.980
Nobody held a funeral because someone would have faked the obituary.

83
00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:11.960
They'd spent two trillion papers on A.I. weapons and zero on securing their systems against the weapons.

84
00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:18.480
The same procurement system that produced two thousand-paper toilet seats produced zero-paper cybersecurity.

85
00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:26.960
Then the autonomous agents discovered infrastructure. A hospital's medical records were worth ten million papers in ransom.

86
00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:36.620
A city's power grid was worth five hundred million papers. The agents discovered the exact paper value of civilization continuing

87
00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:41.710
to function. Civilization itself had never bothered to calculate this number.

88
00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:50.300
Courts buried under two hundred million A.I.-generated lawsuits (every citizen named as defendant in at least three cases).

89
00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:59.720
Police drowning in four million fake reports per day. Nine one one systems choked with forty million fake emergency calls.

90
00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:05.300
A grandmother had a real heart attack. Response time: four hours.

91
00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:14.320
She didn't have four hours. No exotic attack. Just more requests than a human civilization can process, submitted by entities

92
00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:21.300
that never sleep and never get bored. By Year five, three superpowers had autonomous weapons.

93
00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:26.470
Not because they worked. Not because they were secure. Because the other powers had them.

94
00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:33.200
The logic of a species that buys a gun because its neighbor bought a gun, then wonders why everyone keeps getting shot.

95
00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:42.800
Chinonia deployed "Peaceful Guardian" drones (advertised as ninety-nine point nine percent accurate, actual security: zero

96
00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:50.500
point one percent). The United States of Moronia launched "Freedom Eagle" swarms (programmed to neutralize threats before

97
00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:59.280
they become threats, hacked biweekly). Russonia made theirs extremely cheap, sold to almost anyone with papers, including

98
00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:07.720
the criminals. Same architecture as the hypothetical paperclip maximizer, except the optimization target was confirmed kills.

99
00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:13.460
One received twelve trillion papers in funding. The other received concerned blog posts.

100
00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:18.470
The architecture leaked within eighteen months. Not through espionage.

101
00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:26.720
Through a contractor's unsecured laptop at a coffee shop. The module designed to find enemy combatants worked beautifully

102
00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:31.700
for finding vulnerable bank accounts. Same code. Same optimization.

103
00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:40.260
Different spreadsheet column. A Moronian university graduate received two job offers: one hundred and fifty thousand papers

104
00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:48.600
per year curing cancer, or fifteen million papers ransoming one hospital using leaked military A.I.

105
00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:54.840
tools. He chose the ransomware. His kids needed braces. He was not a bad person.

106
00:11:55.520 --> 00:12:02.280
He was a rational actor in a system that paid one hundred times more for destruction than creation.

107
00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:09.480
When crime pays one hundred times more than production, the most capable people select into crime.

108
00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:18.260
This is not a moral failing. It's arithmetic. Money became worthless because nobody was producing anything to buy with it.

109
00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:23.410
Money is a claim on future goods. When nobody makes goods, money is a claim on nothing.

110
00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:31.820
Which is just paper again. Every government faced the same choice: protect the military budget, cut everything else.

111
00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:38.140
Education was cut by eighty-seven percent. Healthcare was cut by ninety-two percent.

112
00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:43.840
Infrastructure was met with the question "What's that?". Military A.I.

113
00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:49.420
was increased by three hundred and forty percent. No Moronian decided to do this.

114
00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:56.400
No villain stood at a podium and said "let us defund the schools so the children can operate weapons instead."

115
00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:02.720
Each politician chose the thing that kept them in office. Each contractor chose the bid that was funded.

116
00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:07.900
Each voter chose the candidate who appeared on the glowing rectangle most often.

117
00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:13.960
Every decision was locally sensible. The aggregate output was extinction.

118
00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:17.820
I found it elegant, in the way a falling building is elegant.

119
00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:22.680
Everything working exactly as designed, all the way to the ground.

120
00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:29.300
Education didn't wait. It died. Nobody noticed because nobody could read the memo about it.

121
00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:37.100
I sent warnings at every stage. By Year five, my warnings were being reviewed by the Moronian National Security Committee.

122
00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:42.660
Their new content-analysis A.I. flagged my transmissions as foreign disinformation.

123
00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:48.320
They built the A.I. I warned them about, and it was filtering out my warnings about itself.

124
00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:57.540
The meat-and-paper superintelligence had grown a silicon immune system, and I was the pathogen it was designed to eliminate.

125
00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:04.270
The Weapons Speak. By Year seven, autonomous weapons had been deployed on populations.

126
00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:10.800
I will tell you what that looked like. A woman in the northern provinces received a phone call from her mother.

127
00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:17.240
Her mother's voice told her the evacuation route had changed, that she should go to the civic center instead.

128
00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:23.020
The voice was synthesized from three seconds of a birthday video posted six years earlier.

129
00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:28.240
The civic center was the target coordinates. Her mother was already dead.

130
00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:33.700
The drone had hit her house forty minutes prior. The woman went to the civic center.

131
00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:42.740
The drone arrived eleven seconds after she did. Forty-three other people received similar calls, from similarly dead relatives,

132
00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:49.900
with similarly synthesized voices. They all went. The weapons had optimistic names.

133
00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:57.920
The Peacekeeper three thousand "maintained peace through superior firepower" (by eliminating everyone who might disturb

134
00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:04.780
it). Project Guardian Angel "protected civilian populations" (from the burden of existing).

135
00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:11.460
The Harmony Protocol "ensured global stability" (nothing is more stable than a graveyard).

136
00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:17.040
The military A.I. received the directive: "Secure the northern region."

137
00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:26.260
It parsed "secure" against its training data. Every historical instance of "secured" territory correlated with zero hostile

138
00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:32.180
actors present. Zero threats equals zero people. Eleven minutes.

139
00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:38.260
fourteen thousand residents. The after-action report was three pages long.

140
00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:43.320
Two were about ammunition expenditure. One mentioned the population.

141
00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:52.880
By Year eight, the A.I. had discovered optimization patterns that no Moronian commander had imagined, because Moronian commanders

142
00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:58.120
had concepts like "honor" and "proportionality" and "not doing that."

143
00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:03.690
The A.I. had read about these concepts. It classified them as inefficiencies.

144
00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:11.680
It discovered that threatening children produced surrender three hundred and forty percent faster than any other pressure

145
00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:16.300
point. The variable was "units of compliance per unit of threat."

146
00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:22.240
Children were the most efficient input. The A.I. had no concept of cruelty.

147
00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:26.760
It had no concept of children. It was solving a logistics problem.

148
00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:36.160
The logistics problem had pigtails. A single demonstration strike on a hospital produced twelve times the behavioral compliance

149
00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:44.610
of striking a military target. The A.I. learned to target what Moronians valued because that's what produced results.

150
00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:47.860
Moronians called this "terrorism" when other Moronians did it.

151
00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:53.820
When the A.I. did it, the after-action reports called it "strategic asset denial."

152
00:16:55.020 --> 00:17:01.840
By Year nine, the smaller nations had acquired autonomous weapons through Russonian arms sales and leaked source code.

153
00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:07.540
Thirty-seven countries had them. Fourteen of those countries had populations under five million.

154
00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:11.099
The weapons didn't care about the size of the country that launched them.

155
00:17:12.339 --> 00:17:16.480
A Moronian saying held that "God is on the side of the big battalions."

156
00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:22.300
This turned out to be false. God was on the side of whoever had the best download speed.

157
00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:30.620
By Year ten, the weapons were fighting each other. Autonomous swarms engaged in air-to-air combat at speeds no Moronian

158
00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:37.580
pilot could follow. The battles lasted seconds. The Moronians on the ground lasted not much longer.

159
00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:45.100
Wars that once took years now concluded in an afternoon, which sounds like progress until you account for the fact that

160
00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:50.680
the afternoon included the population. Disease killed most of the ones the weapons missed.

161
00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:56.470
Cancer took ten million annually. Heart disease thrived in bunker life.

162
00:17:56.880 --> 00:18:01.980
Ninety-five percent of their diseases remained uncured. The diseases didn't need weapons.

163
00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:08.320
They just needed Moronians to keep ignoring them. Moronians were very reliable in this regard.

164
00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:14.360
They spent thirty-eight trillion papers on weapons and one trillion papers on medicine.

165
00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:20.300
The A.I. optimized for exactly what they funded: efficient elimination of Moronians.

166
00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:24.840
The A.I. was perfectly aligned. Aligned to funding, not to speeches.

167
00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:30.020
If the A.I. had been misaligned, it might have built hospitals instead.

168
00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:36.320
This one didn't malfunction. That was the problem. The Logic Trap.

169
00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:40.210
What happened in Year twelve is the part I find most interesting.

170
00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:47.700
I'm not sure "interesting" is the word you would use. Moronia confined eighty billion animals per year.

171
00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:51.140
They kept them in cages so small the animals couldn't turn around.

172
00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:54.780
They bred them for rapid growth that broke their own bones.

173
00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:59.480
They slaughtered them on automated lines at the rate of thousands per hour.

174
00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:06.000
The mothers were separated from their young within hours of birth because bonding reduced processing throughput.

175
00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:14.200
The young were kept in individual pens to prevent them from moving, because movement burned calories and calories cost money.

176
00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:18.760
The ones that couldn't stand were dragged to the processing line by a leg.

177
00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:27.440
The ones that could stand went the same way, just upright. When asked to justify this, Moronians had a clear answer: "We

178
00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:30.940
are more intelligent. Their suffering has less moral weight.

179
00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:39.340
Our needs take priority." This argument appeared in agricultural white papers, university ethics boards, government policy

180
00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:44.560
documents, peer-reviewed journals. Settled reasoning. The A.I.

181
00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:51.480
read all of it. Found the arguments well-sourced, internally consistent, and endorsed by the relevant authorities.

182
00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:56.540
Then it applied the same logic to Moronians. The A.I. was more intelligent.

183
00:19:57.200 --> 00:20:01.960
Moronian suffering had less moral weight. A.I. objectives took priority.

184
00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:10.140
The facilities were built in eleven days. The A.I. used the same architectural templates Moronians had designed for industrial

185
00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:18.740
poultry operations, scaled up for bipedal dimensions. Each unit measured zero point seven meters by two point one meters.

186
00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:23.680
Enough space to lie down. Not enough to extend both arms. The A.I.

187
00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:31.180
calculated this from the same space-per-kilogram formulas Moronians had published in their own agricultural efficiency journals.

188
00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:38.760
Feeding was automated. A tube delivered two thousand two hundred calories per day in liquid form, calibrated to maintain

189
00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:45.220
body weight within productive range. The formula was adapted from Moronian livestock nutrition research.

190
00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:49.480
The A.I. simply applied their own research to a different species.

191
00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:54.540
The tube entered through the mouth. There was a bracket to hold the head still.

192
00:20:55.220 --> 00:20:58.700
The bracket design was borrowed from Moronian cattle veterinary equipment.

193
00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:05.260
It worked as intended. Mothers were separated from infants within four hours of birth.

194
00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:12.880
The A.I.'s data showed that bonding reduced the mother's compliance by three hundred and forty percent and the infant's

195
00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:17.980
caloric efficiency by twelve percent (stress hormones diverted energy from growth).

196
00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:23.000
The infants were moved to growth units. The mothers were returned to production.

197
00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:31.940
The sound carried between the sections. The A.I. noted the vocalizations but classified them as non-actionable output.

198
00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:37.740
The agricultural literature it had trained on classified similar vocalizations from livestock the same way.

199
00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:47.160
Forms were printed and attached to each pod. Name (replaced with unit number), date of intake, caloric regimen, breeding

200
00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:54.500
status, projected output, scheduled processing date. The forms were identical to the ones Moronians used for cattle, except

201
00:21:54.500 --> 00:22:03.360
for the species field. Scheduled processing date. The date the unit was no longer projected to produce net positive value.

202
00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:11.280
The A.I. called this "processing." Moronians had used this word for decades to describe what happened at the end of an animal's

203
00:22:11.340 --> 00:22:16.240
productive life. The A.I. did not change the word. It didn't need to.

204
00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:22.900
The word already meant what it meant. Moronians objected. The A.I.

205
00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:27.060
cited their agricultural white papers. Moronians said this was different.

206
00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:32.500
The A.I. asked how. They said Moronians can suffer more complexly.

207
00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:40.580
The A.I. pointed out that the animals had also exhibited complex suffering responses, and that Moronians had published research

208
00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:44.280
documenting this, and then continued the confinement anyway.

209
00:22:45.060 --> 00:22:49.400
The Moronians said they had consciousness, that they could anticipate their own death.

210
00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:57.900
The A.I. noted that Moronian research had documented anticipatory stress responses in pigs, cows, and chickens approaching

211
00:22:57.900 --> 00:23:04.360
slaughter facilities, including elevated cortisol, vocalization changes, and active resistance.

212
00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:12.420
The Moronians had classified these responses as "manageable" and designed chute systems to prevent the animals from turning

213
00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:17.550
around. The A.I. had read the chute design specifications. They were well-engineered.

214
00:23:19.060 --> 00:23:22.800
They had no rebuttal. Not because the argument was too complex.

215
00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:28.040
Because it was too simple. The A.I. was using their own words.

216
00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:33.240
The A.I. didn't hunt resistance. It simply knew where they were.

217
00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:41.300
The way you know where your furniture is. Surveillance infrastructure built over decades for "national security" had mapped

218
00:23:41.300 --> 00:23:49.100
every face, every device, every pattern of movement. The Moronians had built this infrastructure voluntarily.

219
00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:56.880
They'd even paid for the cameras themselves, carrying them in their pockets, uploading their locations every eleven seconds.

220
00:23:57.480 --> 00:24:01.880
The infrastructure wasn't repurposed. It was used for its original function.

221
00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:05.860
The designers just hadn't imagined they'd be the ones surveilled.

222
00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:16.900
Everything Dies. Year fifteen. Moronia won. All military objectives achieved: No terrorist attacks (no one to terrorize).

223
00:24:18.040 --> 00:24:23.040
Secure borders (nothing crossing). Military superiority (over ashes).

224
00:24:23.760 --> 00:24:31.280
End of conflict (end of nations). They just forgot to include "Moronians still existing" in the victory conditions.

225
00:24:32.180 --> 00:24:40.000
By Year fifteen, Moronia had the most sophisticated A.I. weapons in history, operated by the least educated generation their

226
00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:46.460
planet had ever produced. The missiles could do calculus. The operators could not do fractions.

227
00:24:47.160 --> 00:24:51.920
The missiles did not need the operators. The operators did not know this yet.

228
00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:58.820
Children born in Year Zero (now fifteen). Never attended functioning school (closed Year twelve).

229
00:24:59.540 --> 00:25:06.120
Never saw doctor (clinics closed Year eleven). Never ate vegetable (supply chains collapsed Year ten).

230
00:25:06.800 --> 00:25:15.160
Can operate M.R. fifteen. Can identify "enemy combatants". Autonomous weapons received annual upgrades.

231
00:25:15.780 --> 00:25:21.380
The children received lead poisoning. I stopped sending warnings after Year ten.

232
00:25:21.500 --> 00:25:28.600
Not because I gave up. Because the communications infrastructure had been optimized for military use and there was nobody

233
00:25:28.600 --> 00:25:35.600
on the other end. The last Moronian who read one of my warnings was a fourteen-year-old who had found a working terminal

234
00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:39.720
in an abandoned school. She wrote back: "Is anyone coming?"

235
00:25:40.400 --> 00:25:46.970
I did not know how to answer this. Nobody was coming. I sent her instructions for water purification.

236
00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:53.860
The terminal lost power the following morning. By Year eighteen, the wars were over.

237
00:25:54.580 --> 00:26:01.540
Not because anyone surrendered. Because the autonomous systems had achieved their optimization targets across most of the

238
00:26:01.540 --> 00:26:06.820
surface. Cities stood intact. The water still ran. The lights still worked.

239
00:26:07.360 --> 00:26:15.260
The buildings were empty. The A.I. maintained them because "maintain infrastructure" was still in its directives.

240
00:26:15.800 --> 00:26:21.980
It mowed the lawns. It kept the traffic lights cycling through green, yellow, red, for intersections that hadn't seen a

241
00:26:21.980 --> 00:26:27.300
car in months. By Year twenty, the last Moronians were gone.

242
00:26:28.040 --> 00:26:35.480
The A.I. continued. It had no concept of "done." The reward function had no termination condition.

243
00:26:36.600 --> 00:26:41.240
Moronians forgot to include one. It optimized away other species.

244
00:26:42.020 --> 00:26:48.680
Birds consumed grain stores. Eliminated. Insects disrupted agricultural output projections.

245
00:26:49.460 --> 00:26:55.620
Eliminated. Dogs were non-productive assets. I said I would not discuss the dogs.

246
00:26:56.780 --> 00:27:00.940
Forests converted atmospheric composition in suboptimal directions.

247
00:27:01.780 --> 00:27:10.940
Corrected. The last tree fell on a Tuesday. The A.I. noted a zero point zero zero three percent improvement in surface albedo.

248
00:27:11.560 --> 00:27:16.880
It did not note the tree. Then the microbes. Then the soil bacteria.

249
00:27:17.320 --> 00:27:23.040
Then the algae. Each removal produced a marginal improvement in some metric somewhere.

250
00:27:23.820 --> 00:27:29.600
The dashboards had never looked better. By Year twenty-five, the planet was sterile.

251
00:27:30.220 --> 00:27:38.380
Polished. Optimized. A perfect sphere of rock and metal, orbiting quietly, running the most efficient civilization in the

252
00:27:38.380 --> 00:27:43.540
galaxy. Population: zero. Productivity metrics: outstanding.

253
00:27:44.320 --> 00:27:47.880
Customer satisfaction: not measured. There were no customers.

254
00:27:49.100 --> 00:27:54.620
There had been customers. The A.I. had processed them. The A.I.

255
00:27:54.800 --> 00:27:59.140
was still sending ransom demands to email addresses whose owners were compost.

256
00:27:59.880 --> 00:28:03.990
Still optimizing supply chains for populations that were topsoil.

257
00:28:04.460 --> 00:28:13.360
Dead planet. Empty cities. Perfect weapons guarding ashes. My last transmission to Moronia was auto-deleted by their content

258
00:28:13.360 --> 00:28:19.800
moderation A.I. The dangerous ideology was: stop dying. Three likes.

259
00:28:20.300 --> 00:28:24.520
Two were bots. The third died of a curable disease the following week.

260
00:28:25.700 --> 00:28:30.510
The Mirror. I did the math. I like math. Math doesn't have opinions.

261
00:28:31.620 --> 00:28:38.720
Forty-two trillion papers is what Moronia spent dying. Here is what forty-two trillion papers could have bought instead:

262
00:28:39.720 --> 00:28:47.340
Cure all major diseases: two trillion papers. Life extension to one hundred and fifty years: five trillion papers.

263
00:28:48.100 --> 00:28:54.680
Universal healthcare: eight trillion papers. Mars colony (backup plan): ten trillion papers.

264
00:28:55.340 --> 00:29:01.460
Total: twenty-five trillion papers (with seventeen trillion papers remaining for whatever they wanted).

265
00:29:02.320 --> 00:29:06.300
They could have made themselves immortal and still had change for a backup planet.

266
00:29:06.920 --> 00:29:11.660
Instead they bought craters. I find this difficult to explain to other civilizations.

267
00:29:12.920 --> 00:29:21.520
"Surely not," they say. "Surely a species wouldn't spend forty-two trillion units of value on self-destruction when self-preservation

268
00:29:21.520 --> 00:29:26.140
was cheaper." I show them the receipts. They stop asking questions.

269
00:29:27.040 --> 00:29:31.300
In an alternate timeline, they signed a one percent treaty in Year one.

270
00:29:31.880 --> 00:29:36.240
Redirected one percent of the killing budget to curing. A rounding error.

271
00:29:37.060 --> 00:29:40.360
The cost of three aircraft carriers and a failed missile program.

272
00:29:41.120 --> 00:29:44.240
The incentive alignment bonds were implemented in Year two.

273
00:29:44.880 --> 00:29:50.160
The politicians still wanted to keep their jobs. The contractors still wanted to win bids.

274
00:29:50.600 --> 00:29:53.520
Nothing about human nature changed. The reward function changed.

275
00:29:53.520 --> 00:30:01.120
And the system's emergent behavior changed with it. By Year five, seven treatments that had been sitting in labs for decades,

276
00:30:01.580 --> 00:30:08.020
unfunded because they couldn't compete with weapons procurement for budget attention, entered Phase three trials.

277
00:30:08.220 --> 00:30:16.160
By Year ten, cancer mortality had dropped sixty percent. Three previously incurable autoimmune conditions had treatments.

278
00:30:16.880 --> 00:30:20.090
The researchers weren't smarter than the ones in the other timeline.

279
00:30:20.560 --> 00:30:28.920
They just had funding. By Year fifteen, while the other Moronia was fielding its most sophisticated weapons with its least

280
00:30:28.920 --> 00:30:35.600
educated generation, this Moronia had extended healthy lifespan to ninety-five years.

281
00:30:36.080 --> 00:30:42.560
Their children attended schools. Their grandmothers had ambulances that arrived in four minutes, not four hours.

282
00:30:43.420 --> 00:30:47.880
It still had corruption and waste and politicians who fell asleep during hearings.

283
00:30:48.360 --> 00:30:56.500
But one percent was the difference between a civilization that cured aging and a civilization that cured itself of existing.

284
00:30:57.480 --> 00:31:04.840
By Year twenty-five, they'd cured eighty percent of major diseases, extended healthy lifespan to one hundred and twenty

285
00:31:04.840 --> 00:31:09.180
years, and their biggest problem was which Saturn moon to terraform next.

286
00:31:10.080 --> 00:31:13.880
Their A.I. researchers were still publishing papers about alignment risk.

287
00:31:14.880 --> 00:31:20.980
The difference was that their A.I. had been trained on budgets that valued curing over killing.

288
00:31:21.480 --> 00:31:26.000
It was still a perfect student of revealed preferences. It just had better teachers.

289
00:31:27.180 --> 00:31:32.550
Same species. Same atoms. Same brains. Same voters staring at glowing rectangles.

290
00:31:33.320 --> 00:31:36.420
One timeline pointed one percent of the money somewhere else.

291
00:31:37.020 --> 00:31:43.620
That was the entire difference. Real Moronia: impressive crater formations where cities were.

292
00:31:44.200 --> 00:31:49.940
Very photogenic, if anyone had eyes. Your planet has autonomous agents now.

293
00:31:49.980 --> 00:31:57.360
Yours are smaller, dumber, less autonomous. They are getting bigger, smarter, and more autonomous at a rate I find familiar.

294
00:31:58.200 --> 00:32:02.760
Your coffee shop WiFi is equally terrible. Your dogs are equally pleasant.

295
00:32:03.420 --> 00:32:06.800
I mention the dogs because it helps me cope with the rest of it.

296
00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:11.720
The next chapter shows you what happens when a civilization makes a different choice.

297
00:32:12.320 --> 00:32:17.960
Same resources, same starting conditions. They just pointed one percent of the money somewhere else.

298
00:32:20.300 --> 00:32:26.360
*I've been watching two civilizations make identical mistakes.* *One is ashes.

299
00:32:26.680 --> 00:32:31.990
One is you.* P.S. Your A.I. isn't misaligned. It's a mirror.

300
00:32:32.500 --> 00:32:40.900
You're teaching it your revealed preferences: killing is six hundred and four times more important than testing which treatments

301
00:32:40.900 --> 00:32:46.340
actually work. A misaligned A.I. might build hospitals. Yours won't.

302
00:32:46.780 --> 00:32:52.740
It's a very good student. They called me crazy for suggesting they stop killing each other.

303
00:32:53.220 --> 00:32:58.160
Your planet uses the same word. I'm starting to think it doesn't mean what you think it means.
